!!! Mnemonic for the digits 1-9
;pa re ci vo mu xa ze bi so:__purci ve mixyzbasu__ ''(see [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/lojban/message/8267)''
*] I rather doubt someone could remember the word ''mixyzbasu'' but not remember ''muxazebiso''. I originally learned the digits by chanting them to myself in a rhythm, taking advantage of the fact that they rhyme.But these associations also helped:
       no    "nothing"
       pa    "primary"
       re    2nd note of the scale
       ci    C is the third letter
       vo    sounds like "four"
       mu    The mental image of a cow saying "five" was enough to remember it.
       xa    The Devil laughing diabolically: "xa xa xa..."
       ze    sounds like "seven"
       bi    A capital B looks like an 8
       so    9 is the largest (decimal) digit... but so what?

       ((rab.spir))

* Now, if you could get me some for the hex digits!  (hey, I may be opposed to making it default, but they're handy.  I kind of like ''vai mentu'' for 15 minutes, too).
